Subject: [PATCH] webui: use Referrer-Policy same-origin so Firefox keeps real Origin

The console served `Referrer-Policy: no-referrer` on every response.
Per the Fetch standard ("append a request Origin header"), when the
request's referrer policy is no-referrer the Origin header of a
non-CORS-mode request (the console uses fetch mode:'same-origin') is
serialized as the string "null". Firefox implements this; Chromium
currently still sends the real origin, which is why only Firefox hits
the admin API's sameOrigin() check and gets 403 "仅支持同源控制台请求"
on /admin/api/login.

Switch the header to `same-origin`: cross-site navigations still get
no Referer, while the console's own same-origin POSTs carry the real
Origin and pass the CSRF check unchanged. The sameOrigin() logic and
its tests (Origin:null without same-origin metadata is still rejected)
are untouched.

Verified against rev e0183ac0981d07c6a916c2fc81716db5d9e8cdc7:
go test ./... passes; patched binary serves `Referrer-Policy:
same-origin`, same-origin login returns 200, spoofed `Origin: null`
still returns 403.
---
--- a/cmd/server/main.go
+++ b/cmd/server/main.go
@@ -142,7 +142,10 @@
 		}()
 		r.Body = http.MaxBytesReader(w, r.Body, maxBodyBytes)
 		w.Header().Set("X-Content-Type-Options", "nosniff")
-		w.Header().Set("Referrer-Policy", "no-referrer")
+		// same-origin keeps the real Origin on the console's own POSTs;
+		// no-referrer makes Firefox serialize Origin as "null" (Fetch spec),
+		// which the admin sameOrigin check rejects with 403.
+		w.Header().Set("Referrer-Policy", "same-origin")
 		path := strings.TrimRight(r.URL.Path, "/")
 		if path == "" {
 			path = "/"
